@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+.. zephyr:code-sample:: blinky-hello
+   :name: Blinky + Hello World
+   :relevant-api: gpio_interface
+
+   Blink an LED and periodically print "hello, world" to the console.
+
+Overview
+********
+
+This sample combines the classic :zephyr:code-sample:`blinky` and
+:zephyr:code-sample:`hello_world` samples: it toggles an LED using the GPIO
+API and prints an incrementing "hello, world" message to the console on
+every toggle, once a second. It is useful as a quick smoke test that both
+GPIO output and the console UART are working together on a given board.
+
+Requirements
+************
+
+Your board must:
+
+1. Have an LED connected via a GPIO pin (these are called "User LEDs" on
+   many of Zephyr's :ref:`boards`).
+2. Have the LED configured using the ``led0`` devicetree alias.
+3. Have a working console/UART configured.
+
+Building and Running
+*********************
+
+Build and flash the sample as follows, changing ``<board>`` for your board:
+
+.. zephyr-app-commands::
+   :zephyr-app: samples/basic/blinky_hello
+   :board: <board>
+   :goals: build flash
+   :compact:
+
+After flashing, the LED starts to blink and a message is printed to the
+console every second::
+
+   hello, world 0
+   hello, world 1
+   hello, world 2
